## Scope: the MIT grant above covers this plugin's original code only

The two bundled datasets and the third-party dependencies retain their own
licenses.

- **NMRShiftDB2-derived HOSE shift statistics** are a derivative database under
  the **nmrshiftdb2 Database License (ODbL-derived)**. The source file is
  `src/providers/ocl/nmrshiftdb2.database.json`. The package embeds the data in
  `nmrWorker-*.js` and `OclHosePredictor-*.js` at the ZIP root. The license
  permits commercial use and requires share-alike and attribution on
  redistribution, including redistribution of the plugin ZIP. See
  `src/providers/ocl/NMRSHIFTDB2_LICENSE.md` for provenance and the license text.

- **Ilm-NMR-P31-derived ³¹P HOSE shift statistics** are licensed under
  **BSD-3-Clause**, copyright (c) 2026 Robert Geitner. The source file is
  `src/providers/ocl/ilm-nmr-p31.database.json`. The package embeds the data in
  `nmrWorker-*.js` and `OclHosePredictor-*.js` at the ZIP root. See
  `src/providers/ocl/ILM_NMR_P31_LICENSE.md` for the license text.

- **Third-party dependencies** — openchemlib (BSD-3-Clause), zod (MIT) — remain
  under their own terms. See `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.

Nothing in the MIT grant above conveys any right to those materials beyond their
respective licenses.

MIT was chosen deliberately rather than as a default: the nmrshiftdb2 Database
License requires that prediction software relying on the database be under an
OSI-approved license. MIT is OSI-approved and satisfies that condition.
